WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.864
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.864 --> 00:00:10.462
This lesson covers objective 2 point 3.

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:15.327
Given a scenario, select and configure wireless devices and technologies.

00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:22.190
Today's concept: the non-overlapping 2.4 gigahertz channels, and the two kinds of channel interference.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.524
The 2.4 gigahertz band is crowded.

00:00:26.524 --> 00:00:32.950
Channels are only five megahertz apart, but each one is about twenty megahertz wide, so most of them overlap.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.005
The three channels that do not overlap are one, six and eleven.

00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:39.430
Use those for neighbouring access points.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.130
Two things can go wrong.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.866
Co-channel interference is two access points on the same channel.

00:00:45.866 --> 00:00:49.200
They hear each other and take turns, so airtime is shared.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.838
Adjacent channel interference is worse.

00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:57.470
The channels overlap only partly, so the devices cannot decode each other and do not take turns.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.230
The frames just get corrupted.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.950
For the exam, in 2.4 gigahertz the clean channels are one, six and eleven.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.886
Two access points on the same channel take turns, which is co-channel interference.

00:01:11.886 --> 00:01:17.178
Overlapping channels corrupt each other, and that adjacent channel interference is worse.

00:01:17.178 --> 00:01:19.140
That's objective two point three.
